Z||000009||william_thorniii||11-07-2000||01:05 PM||||Haze's,<P>Contact 87EC05 for more information... <P>Here is all that I have:<P>From:  Fiero87EC5@aol.com Save Address - Block Sender <BR> Add Fiero87EC5@aol.com to your Messenger contact list. <BR>To:  mike.hornsby@mindspring.com, cmankins@mindleaders.com, Dalelee22@cs.com, fiero56@hotmail.com, william_thorniii@hotmail.com, bwilburn4@yahoo.com, pierson.m@pg.com, dandc1@hoosierlink.net Save Address <BR>CC:  FieroWife@aol.com Save Address <BR>Subject:  Re: 2000 IndyOhio Christmas Party <BR>Date:  Sat, 4 Nov 2000 08:26:33 EST <BR>Reply Reply All Forward  Delete  Previous Next  Close <P>WOW!  There was an overwhelming enthusiasm to have this thing so I guess I'll <BR>pursue it!   ;-)   Now we need to decide where and when.   <P>WHERE <P>Because of the way some of us are positioned on the map in relation to <BR>others, it's hard to find a "central" location for everyone.¬  I have two <BR>suggestions (MORE ARE WELCOME!). <P>Suggestion #1 comes to you thanks to Dave Gray.¬  Dave called me last night <BR>(Dave, it was great to talk to you again) and extended this offer:¬  His wife <BR>Anita has offered to provide free use of her hotel‚Äôs banquet hall AND free <BR>hotel rooms for us if we drive to Wabash.¬  Now, Wabash is kinda far for most <BR>of us but, when you factor in you only need to pay for food and gas, it has <BR>the potential for being a nice little getaway.¬  Specifically, distances would <BR>look something like this (these numbers are one-way totals): <P>Dale and Christine, Chad and Angie ‚Äì about 200 miles or 5 hours. <BR>Matt (Matt, what is your wife's name?), William and Lindsey, Bill - about 170 <BR>miles or 4 hours. <BR>Scott and Lisa, Drew ‚Äì 150 miles or 3.5 hours. <BR>Mike and Kelly ‚Äì 92 miles or 2.5 hours. <P>‚ÄúThank you‚Äù to Dave and Anita for this extremely generous offer! <P>Suggestion #2 - there's a BIG intersection where I-70 and I-75 meet that has <BR>several restaurants.  A few of those include: <P>Cracker Barrel - 7171 Miller Lane <BR>Olive Garden - 7500 Poe Avenue <BR>Cooker - 7580 Poe Avenue <BR>Joe's Crab Shack - 6834 Miller Lane <BR>Bob Evan's - 7400 Miller Lane <BR>Red Lobster - 7615 Poe Avenue <BR>Damon's - 4120 Little York Road <BR>Bennigan's - 7260 Miller Road <P>Chad, Angie, Lisa and I met at the Cracker Barrel back in May before heading <BR>to Indy to meet Mike and Kelly at the time trials. <P>This intersection, though not really "centrally" located for all of us, is <BR>fairly straightforward to get to and offers many choices.  Also, except for <BR>the Starcher's and the Hornsby's, drive time is under two hours.  <BR>Specifically, durations would look something like this (these numbers are <BR>one-way totals): <P>Dale and Christine  - about 135 miles or 2.5 hours. <BR>Mike and Kelly - about 120 miles or 2.25 hours. <BR>Matt (Matt, what is your wife's name?) - about 75 miles or 1.5 hours. <BR>Chad and Angie - about 70 miles or 1.5 hours. <BR>Bill - about 58 miles or 1.25 hours. <BR>Drew, William and Lindsey, Lisa and I - 1 hour. <P>Again, these are just suggestions.  Lisa and I are more than willing to drive <BR>just about anywhere.  If you have a better idea, please respond to one of us <BR>(we'll be the focal points for this) and we'll gather votes. <P>Also, children are more than welcome, but I doubt we'll bring our monsters! <P>WHEN <P>The responses I received, for the most part, showed a pretty open month for <BR>everyone.  However, I thought it'd be nice to "kill two birds with one stone" <BR>by having this around Mike's birthday.  So, and again this is just a <BR>suggestion, I propose we have it on the weekend of December 16th.¬  If we go <BR>to Wabash, we could say meet up there in the afternoon, get settled, meet for <BR>dinner that evening, maybe dancing and drinks afterwards, then leave the <BR>following morning.¬  If we do the restaurant thing, I‚Äôd say around 4PM on that <BR>Saturday afternoon.  I suggest this because a few of you have long drives <BR>afterwards and I don't want to be sending you home late.  Of course, if you <BR>would like, you may spend the night at our place (we could retire back at our <BR>place for drinks and playing cards) - but that's a separate discussion. <P>Cast your votes (or other suggestions)! <P>Lisa and Scott <P>In a message dated 11/1/00 3:48:31 PM Eastern Standard Time, Fiero87EC5 <BR>writes: <P>Call me crazy but I'm actually going to try to get all of us together before <BR>Christmas for a little party.  In order to do so, I need some info. <P>If interested in getting together, let me know what weekends are open for <BR>you during the month of December and how far you'd be willing to drive.  <BR>Also, give me some ideas for where to hold this thing.  Would you prefer a <BR>banquet hall?  A restaurant?  A nice hotel? <P>Finally, we need to determine a geographical location for the get-together. <BR> What do all of you suggest?  We've got Dale and Christine in northern <BR>Ohio, Dave and Anita in northern Indiana, Mike and Kelly in central <BR>Indiana, both Matt's and Bill's families in southern Ohio, and the rest of <BR>us in "central" Ohio.  What's a good location for this much distance <BR>between us? <P>We've got at least a month to put this thing together and Lisa and I are <BR>volunteering to be the focal points for it.  If you have suggestions, <BR>comments, questions, concerns, etc., please email or phone us <BR>(phone number has been removed...wtt3). <P>Get your answers back to us as soon as you can. <P>Lisa and Scott <P>||||reg||14
